    {
      "id": "ref-concise",
      "kind": "concise_reference",
      "text": "Non-contrast CT shows no intracranial hemorrhage. There is loss of grey-white differentiation in the left insula and lentiform nucleus with a hyperdense left MCA. In this clinical setting the leading diagnosis is an acute left MCA territory infarct. This is an emergency: I would obtain an immediate CT angiogram of the head and neck to look for a large-vessel occlusion and call the stroke team directly. The CT angiogram shows occlusion of the left M1 segment, which I would communicate immediately and directly as a potential thrombectomy case.",
      "coversElementIds": [
        "e-no-hemorrhage",
        "e-hypodensity",
        "e-dense-mca",
        "e-laterality",
        "e-diagnosis",
        "e-next-imaging",
